  "problem_id": "JSP-000346 / Erdos 421",
  "scope": "For the original distinct-block-product condition, M=floor(sqrt N) satisfies M <= E(N)+(L-1) whenever M < (L+1)!, and M <= E(N)+floor(log_2 M) for every N. No density hypothesis. The earlier coefficient-one/fourth-root and weaker local half-root bounds are retained. Neither density-one existence nor optimality is claimed.",
